    "meaning": "Exact rational vertices, determinant/volume and polynomial simplex moment formula, rational directed enclosures and boundary sign rules.",
    "raw_excerpt": "The finite integrations use rational boxes or rational polytopes.\r\nFor a polytope given by affine inequalities, every possible active\r\nbasis is solved exactly, and each resulting vertex is tested against\r\nevery original inequality.  Boundedness and the face incidences are\r\nverified before a pulling triangulation is formed.  Polynomial\r\nmoments are then exact: on a $d$-simplex $T$ with barycentric\r\ncoordinates $\\lambda_0,\\ldots,\\lambda_d$,\r\n\\begin{equation}\r\n \\int_T\\prod_{j=0}^d\\lambda_j^{\\alpha_j}\\,dx\r\n =d!\\operatorname{vol}(T)\r\n   \\frac{\\prod_{j=0}^d\\alpha_j!}{(d+\\sum_j\\alpha_j)!}.\r\n \\label{num:simplex-moment}\r\n\\end{equation}\r\nRational lower or upper bounds for the remaining kernel factors,\r\ntogether with these moments and \\eqref{num:log-enclosure}, give the\r\nrequired integral enclosure.  A boundary box in a negative-cost upper\r\nintegral is retained with an upper bound for its whole contribution.\r\nIn a positive saving, a box may instead be omitted after establishing\r\nthat its omitted contribution is nonnegative.  These two rules have\r\ndifferent signs and are used separately.\r\n",
    "raw_excerpt_sha256": "febe0ee80cb3b3ad4b507386b893974b3e437d58a247156ed01d340b70df7842"
  },
